<title>POLAND: Farm Food falls 10 pct in profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Farm Food falls 10 pct in profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish meat processing firm Farm Food SA fell the daily maximum 10 percent in active trade to 48.6 zlotys, apparently hit by profit-taking, analysts said.</p>
<p>&quot;The stock had grown a lot recently so it seems it fell for technical reasons,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Farm Food had risen to 59 zlotys from 43.6 zlotys between January 30 and February 18 before its recent slide began.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
